<title>FRANCE: Socialists seek quashing of French pensions bill.</title>
<headline>Socialists seek quashing of French pensions bill.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's opposition Socialist Party will ask the country's highest constitutional authority to annul a bill on the introduction of private pension funds, Socialist party member Marc Massion said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The Socialists would repeal the law if they took power in 1998, he said during a second reading of the text in the Senate, or upper house of parliament.</p>
<p>&quot;Without overstating it, you are dramatically changing our system of social protection...this text is both inegalitarian for our people and dangerous for the social security regime, we will refer it to the constitutional council,&quot; Massion said.</p>
</text>
